Version 3.2.1
03.08.2026

Fixed: Dovetail Cutouts doing nothing due to an inverted condition from a previous refactor
-----------------------------
Version 3.2
31.07.2026

Added: GeoJSON boundary import as a new Terrain map mode, including MultiPolygon (islands/exclaves) support and merging multiple boundary files into one shape (by Louisefeige) (Premium)
Added: Coordinate search with city lookup and lat/lon input, plus new map layers for Browser based Features (Puzzle/Multitile Configurator)
Added: Circle Outer Text shape
Added: Medal handle support for text-based shapes
Added: Shell geometry for text-based shapes (Premium)
Added: Material preview mode in the Puzzle Configurator
Added: Hexagonal and Concentric-Ring puzzle piece shapes in the Puzzle Configurator (Premium)
Added: Shapely/Earcut status indicators and clearer error messages when Shapely fails to load
Added: ARM64 and macOS 10.13 x86_64 wheels for Shapely and Mapbox Earcut
Added: 'Bay' natural features are now fetched and classified as water in OSM data
Added: Puzzle/Multitile Configurator now remembers the selected base map layer across sessions
Added: Puzzle Configurator seed input for reproducible puzzle generation
Added: 'Map Scale Ratio' (1:X) map metadata property, and a matching {scale} code for text-based shapes
Changed: Default terrain source is now Mapterhorn
Changed: Smoother raw OSM element boundaries before extrusion, and fetched OSM polygons are now clipped to the query bbox
Changed: Faster full-ocean tile mesh generation
Changed: Updated projection logic for Ocean creation
Changed: Restructured Shape selection UI
Changed: Improved update checker reliability
Changed: Updated export format handling for terrain-element colors in Paint mode
Changed: Reworked Contour Lines — now subtracts its bands from the map instead of only intersecting, supports real-world-meter distance/offset (elevation-scale aware, enabled by default) alongside mm, generates at the map's own origin instead of the 3D cursor, and warns instead of failing when distance is smaller than thickness
Fixed: Shapely should now be installed correctly and no longer throw errors
Fixed: Ocean creation now supports merging with the map again
Fixed: Steep (60°) walls were incorrectly detected as vertical walls during raycast
Fixed: Trail points bouncing in one direction during Multi-generation
Fixed: Buggy BMesh shapes causing issues with Rivers and unreliable element painting
Fixed: Trails clipping through hills
Fixed: Progress bar/browser window not opening properly in app mode when no Chromium browser is found
Fixed: Spike artifacts on complex GeoJSON boundaries
Fixed: Crash in Separate/Single-Color element mode with exactly one surviving part
Fixed: GPX chain import not working due to a broken condition check
Fixed: Malformed GPX files crashing the addon instead of showing a clear error
Fixed: Incorrect vertex selection/lowest point calculation for Oceans
Fixed: Elevation Range (m) map metadata was inflated by an uncompensated per-vertex Mercator latitude factor baked into terrain height generation, causing incorrect real-world elevation figures away from the equator
Fixed: Duplicate warning messages repeating once per tile when generating a multitile batch
Fixed: Various scaling and logic bugs in the MultiTile Configurator
Fixed: Map picker window could occasionally freeze Blender's input focus on close
-----------------------------
Version 3.1.1
01.07.2026

Added: Mapterhorn terrain tiles — premium terrain elevation source with improved tile fetching and error handling
Added: Coastline/river map size limit — prevents oversized OSM requests for water features
Added: Optional update checker — update check can now be disabled or ignored
Added: Export warnings — shows an error and skips export if no export folder is set
Changed: Single Color Mode now dynamically calculates extrusion heights based on map height
Changed: Reduced parallel Overpass requests to 1 to prevent rate limiting on large maps (HTTP 429)
Changed: Trail stability improvements using the Remesh + Shapely approach
Changed: Buggy terrain fix made optional instead of always applied
Changed: Tile counter added to the debug console during OSM fetching
Changed: Auto-export disabled for multi-tile maps
Fixed: Trail cutting through the map on text-based shapes
Fixed: Buggy Remesh for cutouts deeper than 30mm
Fixed: Some trails not creating cutouts when intersecting other trails
Fixed: Wrong normals on shapes after Grid Fill (causing raycast failures)
Fixed: Trail Raycast default height
Fixed: Post-process operators having the wrong object selected
Fixed: SCM trail origin being placed at world origin
Changed: Single Color Mode boolean changed to Manifold to prevent artifacts when curve touches shape border
-----------------------------
Version 3.1
21.06.2026

Added: Puzzle Configurator — browser-based interface to create custom puzzle maps
Added: Custom input for Road height
Added: Generated-maps counter tracked in Advanced -> Additional Info
Added: File Picker now filters and shows only valid files
Added: Automatic Addon version updater
Added: Russian translation
Changed: Replaced custom geometry processing with a Shapely-based pipeline for all Elements — far more robust and faster than booleans, with fewer vertices and no downsides
Changed: OSM fetching is now parallelized and pre-fetched during the Elevation download — way fewer requests, saving a lot of time for element-heavy maps
Changed: Improved Progress Bar status updates
Changed: Hexagon Outer shape now has 6 text input fields instead of 4
Changed: Minimum required Blender version is now 5.1 instead of 4.5 due to the bundled python wheels
Fixed: GPX import dropping path segments at overlapping points
Fixed: Stray single vertices requiring manual smoothing
Fixed: Elevation cache not being deleted properly
Fixed: Crash when a trail object is empty after a boolean operation
-----------------------------
